  "notes": "St. Anne of the Marrow, the parish church that went down with the old lobe: a white board church, nave 9 x 15 m with lancet windows and a chancel behind (+Z), and a square tower on the front (local -Z), 5 m on a side, with the door, a louvred belfry and corner pinnacles 17.75 m up. Base sea puts its floor a metre under the bay; give it an age so the roof and glass are gone.",
